{title: Rebelled Against the King}
{subtitle: 2 Kings 3:4–5}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Abmaj7/Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb/D]Mesha king [Cm7]of Moab was a sheep breed[Fm]er
He paid [Eb]the king of Israel [Bb]ev[Ab]ery year
A hun[Bb7/Ab]dred thousand [Gm7]lambs was the trib[Fm]ute
And wool from a hundred [Bb]thousand rams
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]But when [Bb/D]Ahab died the [Cm]bond was broken
The [Fm]king of Moab rebelled against Is[Bb]rael
[Ab]The sheep breed[Bb7/Ab]er stopped [Eb/G]his payment
And the sheep [Fm]breeder re[Bb7]fused the heavy [Eb]load
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
The [Cm]tribute of [Bb]lambs was no [Ab]longer [Eb]paid
The [Cm]wool of the [Bb]rams stayed in [Ab]his [Eb]fold
He re[Cm]belled against the [Bb]king of [Ab]Israel
And the [Fm]sheep breeder held his [Bb]ground
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
He re[Fm]belled against [Bb]the [Eb]king
{end_of_verse}
